<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Austria</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Austria is a country in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-europe">Central Europe</a> with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>. It was the hereditary base of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg dynasty</a>, which held the title of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a> for most of the period from the fifteenth century. Austria later formed the core of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austrian-empire">Austrian Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a>, and it took part in the partitions of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/austria.jpg" alt="Austria" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bundesministerium für Landesverteidigung · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Austria.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
